{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And you shall give it.</b> Here Rashi explained that the years of the men are counted according to the count of the years of the world, which begin from Tishrei. One may ask: this works well for the one who says the world was created in Tishrei, but for the one who says the world was created in Nisan, what is there to say? And furthermore, it is difficult, for when Scripture writes ומעלה, we count from a person's birth. Therefore it seems to me that they were counted only once. And since they went up in the second month and would complete twenty years, they likewise gave [the shekel] initially after Yom HaKippurim of the first year. And so too it follows from within Rashi's explanation, who explained above והשנית — that it too was by means of a counting that counted them from when the Tabernacle was erected. And according to this, the count of the shekalim that were in Iyar is equal to those."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "The phrase ומעלה (literally 'and upward') refers to Numbers 1:3, where the Torah counts those 'from twenty years old and upward.' The comment questions why Rashi in Exodus aligns the count with calendar years beginning in Tishrei rather than with each individual's age from birth."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:04:25.720776480Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}